    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Alfajr Alarm works entirely on your device. It has no account, advertising, analytics, telemetry, internet, or location permission. Your selected city, calculation settings, and alarm preferences remain local. Android backup may restore preferences, but never an enabled alarm.</string>
    <string name="licenses_body">Alfajr Alarm is MIT licensed. Prayer-time calculations use Adhan (MIT). The bundled worldwide city data incorporates GeoNames geographical data and is licensed under CC BY 4.0. The GeoNames attribution remains in this app and the third-party notices.</string>
    <string name="troubleshooting_body">If you force-stop the app, Android may suppress scheduled alarms until you open it again. Open Alfajr Alarm after a restart or after changing the clock or time zone. If your device has aggressive battery management, verify one real alarm before relying on it. The app never changes Do Not Disturb or alarm volume for you.</string>
